WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.280 --> 00:00:05.520
This is the Mutual Fund factory, where
all the world’s mutual funds are produced.

00:00:05.520 --> 00:00:11.580
Fund elves wrap stardust, lemondrops and
a nickel in a unicorn bladder, which is then

00:00:11.580 --> 00:00:16.580
delivered via dragon-sled to brokerage firms,
who sell them to customers.

00:00:16.580 --> 00:00:22.920
The customer buries the mutual fund in their
backyard, and after 30 or 40 years, a money

00:00:22.920 --> 00:00:26.290
tree starts blossoming, just in time for retirement.

00:00:26.290 --> 00:00:29.330
Babe, that’s not remotely true.

00:00:29.330 --> 00:00:33.120
I know, but we have to get people excited
about mutual funds somehow.

00:00:33.120 --> 00:00:36.920
They’re an important option in saving for
retirement and most people don’t even know

00:00:36.920 --> 00:00:38.399
what they are!

00:00:38.399 --> 00:00:39.559
Even people who own them…

00:00:39.559 --> 00:00:40.839
like in their 401(k)s!

00:00:40.839 --> 00:00:41.839
Wait…

00:00:41.839 --> 00:00:43.920
401(k)s are mutual funds?

00:00:43.920 --> 00:00:45.320
No, not exactly.

00:00:45.320 --> 00:00:51.230
Let’s start at the beginning.

00:00:55.080 --> 00:01:00.339
A mutual fund is kinda like... a bowl of investment
stew.

00:01:00.339 --> 00:01:04.739
Thousands--or even millions--of investors
pool their money to buy a variety of investments

00:01:04.739 --> 00:01:09.580
(primarily stocks, bonds and currencies) which
are blended together and then divided amongst

00:01:09.580 --> 00:01:10.700
the participants.

00:01:10.700 --> 00:01:15.260
And just like a restaurant serves a lot of
different dishes, mutual funds come in a lot

00:01:15.260 --> 00:01:16.759
of different flavors…

00:01:16.759 --> 00:01:22.100
Some funds focus on a specific sector of the
economy, like Technology, Retail or Agriculture.

00:01:22.100 --> 00:01:27.210
Others focus on specific areas of the world
- “Emerging Markets” refers to developing

00:01:27.210 --> 00:01:28.210
nations.

00:01:28.210 --> 00:01:33.039
And some focus on the size of the companies
- from Large-Cap to Micro-Cap.

00:01:33.039 --> 00:01:37.630
And they can get a lot more customized than
that: The Pax World Global Women’s Equality

00:01:37.630 --> 00:01:41.590
Fund invests in companies that advance the
cause of gender equality.

00:01:41.590 --> 00:01:47.299
Or, for something completely different, the
Vice Fund focuses on tobacco, alcohol, gaming,

00:01:47.299 --> 00:01:49.340
and weapons companies.

00:01:49.340 --> 00:01:53.770
Mutual fund shares are usually inexpensive,
and you get the advantage of diversification

00:01:53.770 --> 00:01:57.100
without having to buy hundreds or thousands
of shares yourself.

00:01:57.100 --> 00:01:58.740
BUT there are costs.

00:01:58.740 --> 00:02:03.929
Every mutual fund has an upkeep fee called
an ANNUAL EXPENSE RATIO, which ranges from

00:02:03.929 --> 00:02:07.469
around 0.1% to 2% of the value per year.

00:02:07.469 --> 00:02:13.040
Some funds also charge an extra fee called
a LOAD when you buy or sell your shares, usually

00:02:13.040 --> 00:02:17.400
between 1% and 5.75% of the sale price.

00:02:17.400 --> 00:02:21.209
You can think of these fees as payment to
the chef who whipped up your dinner.

00:02:21.209 --> 00:02:23.730
Wait… who are these chefs anyway?

00:02:23.730 --> 00:02:26.480
And how are they deciding what ingredients
to use?

00:02:26.480 --> 00:02:31.680
Well, that depends on whether your mutual
fund is ACTIVELY or PASSIVELY managed.

00:02:31.680 --> 00:02:34.960
Active funds are managed by a team of analysts
and traders.

00:02:34.960 --> 00:02:39.760
They try to out-perform the market by carefully
watching economic indicators and picking which

00:02:39.760 --> 00:02:42.209
investments to hold and which to sell.

00:02:42.209 --> 00:02:46.159
Kinda like a celebrity chef who’s always
improvising and changing her recipes based

00:02:46.159 --> 00:02:48.290
on what’s trendy or in season.

00:02:48.290 --> 00:02:52.800
As you can imagine, the fees on actively managed
funds tend to be higher.

00:02:52.800 --> 00:02:56.730
Passive fund managers are more like chefs
who stick to the cookbook.

00:02:56.730 --> 00:03:00.470
Their goal is to match benchmarks, not beat
them.

00:03:00.470 --> 00:03:06.599
For example, an “S&amp;P 500 Index Fund” tries
to mirror the modest but steady growth seen

00:03:06.599 --> 00:03:09.420
in the index of 500 of the biggest companies.

00:03:09.420 --> 00:03:14.489
Passive funds are popular among investors
who believe it’s a losing game to try to

00:03:14.489 --> 00:03:15.580
“beat the market.”

00:03:15.580 --> 00:03:20.670
Because there’s less analysis and fewer
trades, passive funds are cheaper to own.

00:03:20.670 --> 00:03:23.080
Mutual funds are an amazing creation.

00:03:23.080 --> 00:03:28.610
They allow ordinary people to invest like
huge institutions--thousands of holdings,

00:03:28.610 --> 00:03:32.819
diversification--while being easy to use and
letting you express your personal tastes and

00:03:32.819 --> 00:03:33.819
principles.

00:03:33.819 --> 00:03:35.040
But where do you start?

00:03:35.040 --> 00:03:39.590
If you don’t have any mutual fund investments
yet, you might begin by opening an investment

00:03:39.590 --> 00:03:42.060
account with a mutual fund company.

00:03:42.060 --> 00:03:47.120
Their advisors will help you choose funds
that are a good fit for your situation.

00:03:47.120 --> 00:03:51.640
Investors who are a bit savvier and want a
more modern approach are starting to use “Robo-Advisors”

00:03:51.640 --> 00:03:53.140
to invest in mutual funds.

00:03:53.140 --> 00:03:58.230
Basically, you answer a few questions online
and the service automatically constructs a

00:03:58.230 --> 00:04:02.770
personalized portfolio of funds for you and
handles all the trades and holdings.

00:04:02.770 --> 00:04:06.959
Plus their investment minimums are pretty
low, sometimes just $100!

00:04:06.959 --> 00:04:11.240
And if you’re invested in a 401(k) plan
through your work, you already own mutual

00:04:11.240 --> 00:04:12.240
funds!

00:04:12.240 --> 00:04:15.860
And you’re paying fees for an advisor, so
don’t be afraid to contact them and find

00:04:15.860 --> 00:04:18.840
out which funds you own and what your options
are.

00:04:18.840 --> 00:04:21.560
I remember the first time I went to a sushi
restaurant.

00:04:21.560 --> 00:04:25.340
I didn’t recognize a lot of the ingredients
on the menu, and it was a little intimidating.

00:04:25.340 --> 00:04:30.560
But it didn’t take me long to learn what
I liked and I’m so glad I did.

00:04:30.560 --> 00:04:33.420
Like sushi, mutual funds may not be for everyone.

00:04:33.420 --> 00:04:38.150
But everyone should be planning for retirement,
and mutual funds are popular with investors

00:04:38.150 --> 00:04:40.590
of every level for good reason.

00:04:40.590 --> 00:04:43.500
And that’s our two cents!

